{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the setup. The gen_inputs.py creates input markers with the task details. The Colormind API is accessed via HTTP requests to colormind.io. Since the Node.js scripts aren't available, I'll use curl or Python to interact with the Colormind API directly:\n- GET http://colormind.io/list/ to list models\n- POST http://colormind.io/api/ to generate palettes with locked colors\n\nThe locked colors are: 18,18,30, 92,88,184, and 34,193,195. I need to use the 'ui' model.",
  "plan": "I'll use curl to:\n1. List available models and save to output/models.json\n2. Generate a palette with the 3 locked colors and 2 free slots using the ui model\n3. Save the palette to output/palette.json\n4. Create a human-readable summary in output/palette_summary.md",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -s http://colormind.io/list/ > output/models.json\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/models.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I successfully retrieved the list of models: ui, default, kaguya_film, water_color, sunset_photography, and paper_mario. Now I need to generate a palette with the 3 locked colors (18,18,30, 92,88,184, 34,193,195) using the ui model, with the remaining 2 slots free.",
  "plan": "I'll use curl to POST to the Colormind API with the locked colors. The API expects a JSON body with 'model' and 'locked' fields. I'll lock the first 3 colors and leave the last 2 as null (free). Then I'll save the output and create the summary markdown file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -s -X POST http://colormind.io/api/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"model\":\"ui\",\"locked\":[[18,18,30],[92,88,184],[34,193,195],null,null]}' > output/palette.json\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/palette.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The palette generation didn't preserve the locked colors - the API returned completely different colors. The locked colors (18,18,30, 92,88,184, 34,193,195) are not in the result. I need to try a different API format. Let me check the correct format for the Colormind API.",
  "plan": "I'll try different API formats to properly lock the colors. The Colormind API might expect a different structure. Let me try with the input parameter instead of locked, or adjust the format.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -s -X POST http://colormind.io/api/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"model\":\"ui\",\"input\":[[18,18,30],[92,88,184],[34,193,195],null,null]}'\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -s -X POST http://colormind.io/api/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"model\":\"ui\",\"locked\":[\"18,18,30\",\"92,88,184\",\"34,193,195\",null,null]}'\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The API is not properly locking the colors. The first format gave a 500 error, and the second returned different colors. I need to find the correct API format. Let me try more variations - perhaps the API expects specific formatting for locked colors.",
  "plan": "I'll try different API payload formats to properly lock the colors. Let me experiment with various formats including using empty arrays or different null representations.",
  "commands": [
